<title>USA: Wyman-Gordon chairman to retire in October.</title>
<headline>Wyman-Gordon chairman to retire in October.</headline>
<dateline>NORTH GRAFTON, Mass. 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wyman-Gordon Co said Thursday that its chairman, John Nelson, plans to retire effective with the annual shareholders meeting in October.</p>
<p>At that time the board expects to elect David Gruber, currently president and chief executive officer, as chairman, the company said.</p>
<p>Wyman-Gordon makes forgings, investment castings and composite structures for use in the commercial and defense aerospace, commercial power and energy and performance product markets.</p>
